Is there any way to get a lock over 2 different objects together?
I tried to use lock(obj1, obj2){...} but I got this error:

invalid expression term ','


UPDATE:
As many of users told me to try and use just one lock, and I appreciate their advice because it's more preferable most of the time, I just want to show a case in which I think have a lock over 2 objects is more reasonable.
Consider the case of having 2 queues shared among different threads. You need to avoid do Enqueue(item) and Dequeue() simultaneously. Now, at a particular section of your code, you want to get an element from one queue and insert it into the second queue. I know it's possible to do it like:

var itme;
lock(_lock1)
{
    item = q1.Dequeue();
    Monitor.Pulse(_lock1);
}
lock(_lock2)
{
    q2.Enqueue(item);
    Monitor.Pulse(_lock2);
}


But I think get a lock over both _lock1 and _lock2 is more readable and clean.

